# CODEOWNERS — routes review of the listing and the machinery to the maintainer.
#
# What this file does on its own: nothing but request a review. CODEOWNERS is not an
# enforcement mechanism; the enforcement is branch protection on `main`, enabled
# 2026-08-28, which requires a pull request, one approving review, code-owner review,
# and a passing `validate` check before anything merges.
#
# Stated precisely, because an earlier version of this comment claimed a "structural
# guarantee" that did not exist — the rules were described here but never configured,
# so every merge was in fact unreviewed:
#
#   * A pull request cannot be merged without the maintainer's approval and a green
#     `validate`. That part is enforced, not just documented.
#   * The maintainer is a repository admin and can override both, which GitHub records
#     on the push as "Bypassed rule violations". It is an audited escape hatch, not a
#     silent one — the alternative, admin-enforced protection, would lock the sole
#     maintainer out of their own repository, since GitHub does not permit approving
#     one's own pull request.
#   * The daily metadata refresh cannot push to `main` either. It opens a single rolling
#     pull request instead (`chore/metadata-refresh`).
#
# @O0000-code is the repository owner and sole maintainer.

# Default: the owner reviews everything not matched more specifically below.
*                   @O0000-code

# The listing itself — the source of truth. Never changes without human review.
/data/              @O0000-code

# Generated output — should only change via the generator, never hand-edited.
/README.md          @O0000-code
/README.zh-CN.md    @O0000-code

# The machinery: generator, schema, templates, config, CI, and this file.
/scripts/           @O0000-code
/schema/            @O0000-code
/templates/         @O0000-code
/config.yaml        @O0000-code
/.github/           @O0000-code
